---
/*
  TestWebpage — PAGE 2, Why educational email works (/testwebpage/educational/).
  Copy verbatim from 12-BUILD-COPY.md. Box/note markers + question numbers not rendered.
  Buttons: EEC landing + LinkedIn thread are unresolved placeholders (href="#").
*/
import TestLayout from '../../layouts/TestLayout.astro';
---
<TestLayout
  title="Why educational email works — First Action Fix"
  description="A free five-day email course that teaches a problem the buyer already has, and ends at the product."
  active="educational"
>
  <!-- Box 1 — what it is -->
  <section class="hero box">
    <h1>Why educational email works</h1>
    <p class="lead">A free five-day email course that teaches a problem the buyer already has, and ends at the product.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Box 2 — who -->
  <section class="box">
    <p>For construction software where signups arrive and most never reach a second session.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Box 3 — what changes -->
  <section class="box">
    <p>A visitor who would have left leaves an address instead — and comes back taught.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Box 4 — why it works + table -->
  <section class="box">
    <p>Buyers compare across thousands of vendors, jumping tab to tab. Winning that attention with genuine advice — and a contact — is a large gain over a visitor who just left and costs ad rates to reach again. A landing page keeps 2–5%; the course keeps more of the rest, and a known sender reads as safe.</p>

    <!-- Box 4b — table, per 10,000 unique visits -->
    <table>
      <caption>Per 10,000 unique visits</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Per 10,000 unique visits</th><th>Usual</th><th>With the course</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Take the primary door</td><td>200–500</td><td>200–500</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Leave, reachable only at ad rates</td><td>9,500–9,800</td><td>fewer</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Addresses kept</td><td>0</td><td>~200</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <!-- Box 5 — the catch -->
  <section class="box">
    <p>Below ~2,000 sessions a month it recovers a rounding error, and around 400 it is about one conversion a quarter — thin enough that I would usually suggest waiting, and not a case for buying clicks to feed it.</p>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- Box 6 — close -->
  <section class="box">
    <div class="btns">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#">Join the course</a><!-- -> EEC landing (external, other chat) -->
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#">Reply in the DM</a><!-- -> LinkedIn thread -->
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Box 7 — after -->
  <section class="box">
    <p>Five lessons, one a day, each usable on the current trial; the last asks what is still missing.</p>
  </section>
</TestLayout>
